(Bug #77: `append -5 to xs.` answered "Expected value to append" while
 `append {-5} to xs.` - the same tokens, routed to the general primary -
 compiled. `-` is only ever a sign in Vox; subtraction is spelled
 `subtract` or `minus`, so there was nothing for the append slot to
 protect by refusing it.)

a number called n is 5.
a list called xs is [].

append -5 to xs.
append -0.5 to xs.
append -n to xs.
append -9223372036854775808 to xs.

(The neighbours that already worked, still working.)
append {-5} to xs.
append 0 minus 5 to xs.

Print element 1 of xs.
Print element 2 of xs.
Print element 3 of xs.
Print element 4 of xs.
Print element 5 of xs.
Print element 6 of xs.
Exit 0.
